WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:03.750
The savviest movie stars give the people what
they want.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:07.750
And in the late '80s, the people wanted a
sort-of-mystical, stone-faced martial arts

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.850
expert with a ponytail—in other words, Steven
Seagal.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:15.450
"I have something in my pocket right now,
to completely clear up that bruise on your

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.430
forehead."

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.680
"What bruise?"

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:18.220
"Ah!"

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.220
"That bruise."

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:23.080
He ruled the box office for years with huge
hits like Hard to Kill, Above the Law, and

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.119
Under Siege, but tastes change and eventually,
he faded from movie star prominence.

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:29.470
So what ever happened to Steven Seagal?

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.380
He Still Makes Lots Of Movies

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.879
Seagal's contract with Warner Bros. ended
with the release of the environmentally-themed

00:00:35.879 --> 00:00:38.559
thriller Fire Down Below in 1997.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.540
"Cracked my wood, that's no good."

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.780
He still makes action movies, though, it's
just that most of them have gone straight

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.480
to DVD or streaming.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:49.889
In fact, Seagal has churned out more than
30 movies in the last two decades, with awesome

00:00:49.889 --> 00:00:53.549
titles like Urban Justice, Out for a Kill,
and Half Past Dead.

00:00:53.549 --> 00:00:54.149
Awesome.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.300
"We got a problem."

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:57.320
"How do I look?"

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.300
"Like a big fat prom queen."

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.659
Two Cop Shows: One Real, One Fake

00:01:01.659 --> 00:01:06.150
In the late '80s, Jefferson Parish, Louisiana
Sheriff Harry Lee asked Seagal to train his

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:10.150
force in martial arts, eventually enlisting
Seagal as a reserve deputy.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:16.310
In 2009, Seagal's side gig became the basis
for a reality show on A&amp;E called Steven Seagal:

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:17.310
Lawman.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.770
"This is not good."

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:24.480
It was similar to COPS, except that Steven
Seagal was there, which had to be really weird

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.510
for the criminals.

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:26.990
"Steven Seagal!

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:28.420
My wife loves you.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.930
I don't like you, but my wife loves you!"

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:36.140
Sadly, Seagal reportedly resigned from the
force after he found himself the subject of

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:40.610
an internal affairs investigation that, according
to the Phoenix New Times, sought to uncover

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:46.340
the truth about "allegations of --- ----------- and
------ -------." But in 2011, Seagal used

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:50.290
the lemons life gave him to make lemonade
with the action series True Justice, which

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:55.200
he created and starred in as Elijah Kane,
head of an elite undercover Seattle task force.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.780
It ran for 26 episodes on the network Reelz
before being canceled.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.170
Entrepreneur

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:07.670
From 1999 to 2007, Seagal owned a 995-acre
lavender farm in northern California where

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:12.379
he grew the raw materials for Diamond Lotus
Essentials, a line of "therapeutic oils,"

00:02:12.379 --> 00:02:16.750
and he currently owns an estate in California's
Santa Ynez Valley, where he grows Cabernet

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.070
grapes that he then sells to other wineries.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.360
"You've done well."

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:30.900
Plus, there's Steven Seagal's Lightning Bolt,
a line of canned energy drinks that was proudly

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:35.420
marketed as the first of its kind to contain
"Tibetan Goji Berries" and "Asian Cordyceps."

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.220
"It's good to be the king isn't it?

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:43.579
And guess what, this could happen to you,
if you drank Lightning Bolt."

00:02:43.579 --> 00:02:44.959
Real Life Drama

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:46.969
Seagal has been married four times.

00:02:46.969 --> 00:02:51.370
His third and most prominent marriage was
with another nostalgic icon, model and actress

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:55.969
Kelly LeBrock, most famous for being the dream
woman created by teen scientists in Weird

00:02:55.969 --> 00:02:56.969
Science.

00:02:56.969 --> 00:03:00.961
Seagal and LeBrock divorced in 1996 after
he reportedly had an affair with their nanny,

00:03:00.961 --> 00:03:02.480
and she got pregnant.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:08.139
In 2009, he married his personal assistant,
Erdenetuya Batsukh, but a year later, another

00:03:08.139 --> 00:03:13.319
of Seagal's former personal assistants, Kayden
Nguyen, sued Seagal for $1 million, alleging

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:15.209
he harassed and abused her.

00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:19.379
Those allegations were corroborated by two
other female ex-employees who alleged similar

00:03:19.379 --> 00:03:23.080
treatment by the actor, but the suit was dropped
later in the year.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.680
Missed Opportunities

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:29.809
In 2007, Seagal's pal Jackie Chan is rumored
to have suggested that Seagal play the villain

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:30.930
in Rush Hour 3.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:35.389
After that fell through, in 2010 Sylvester
Stallone offered Seagal a part in the action

00:03:35.389 --> 00:03:38.509
flick The Expendables, which was chock full
of 80's action heroes.

00:03:38.509 --> 00:03:42.129
Seagal refused, though, due to a feud with
one of the film's producers, and missed out

00:03:42.129 --> 00:03:45.730
on what would have been one of the biggest
hits of his career.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:46.730
World Citizen

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:51.310
Bizarrely, two of Seagal’s friends are Buddhist
spiritual leader the Dalai Lama...and Russian

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:55.010
president Vladimir Putin, with whom Seagal
is especially close.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:04:01.719
"He is one of the greatest world leaders if
not the greatest world leader alive today."

00:04:01.719 --> 00:04:06.379
In addition, Seagal gained citizenship in
Serbia in January 2016 after offering to set

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:09.870
up a martial arts studio there...to go along
with his blues concerts.

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:12.870
(Steven Seagal plays the blues)

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:16.790
He probably wouldn't be able to live in Serbia,
however, if he followed through on his plans

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:18.700
to someday run for governor of Arizona.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.750
"I think our biggest problem is open borders."

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:22.950
Sorry, Steven.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:25.310
Not every problem can be solved by kicking.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:25.890
"Ow!"

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.900
Or whatever this is.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:32.440
(Steven Seagal plays the blues...again)

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:33.320
Thanks for watching!

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:36.500
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:40.200
And leave us a comment to let us know which
Steven Seagal movie is your favorite, aw ya!

